{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/685081-orpheus-and-wraiths","id":685081,"title":"Orpheus and Wraiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-01T17:48:39-07:00","id":685081,"title":"Orpheus and Wraiths","content":"How do the two mesh together? I understand that Orpheus characters are somehow like living wraiths, but I don't know much beyond that. Can the two use the same Arcanois, is there an underworld and Tempest in Orpheus, do Necropolis have a position on the tourists that are showing up? One last question: how does this mesh with the masquerade/Veil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:16:53-07:00","id":685111,"title":"","content":"As written, Orpheus was released after Wraith's Ends of Empire, and neither seems to mesh well with the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1738-charon","name":"Charon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T18:19:14-07:00","id":685115,"title":"","content":"Wraiths use Acanoi, the ghosts of Orpheus do not. As to a Wraith equivalent of the Masquerade of the Kindred, there is the Stygian Hierarchy's decree of the Dictum Moryuum, prohibiting ghostly interference with the affairs of the living. Orpheus ghosts have no such rule that applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1738-charon","name":"Charon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T19:24:08-07:00","id":685147,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head, so I might get some details wrong...<br /> <br /> Orpheus occurs after metaplot events that change the status of the underworld significantly. Shit gets fucked up, it's unclear quite what happened to all of the Dark Kingdoms but at least parts of them were devastated and seemingly tossed into the Tempest, and the current status of anything past the Shadowlands in Orpheus appears to be sufficiently wrecked and dangerous that the gameline doesn't breach the Stormwall (the Orpheus Group's term for what became of the Shroud, kind of) until Orpheus's own endgame book. It doesn't really address how the wraiths pre-Maelstrom would have received skimmers and sleepers, the living who have discovered means to sort of project their consciousness as a wraith into the Shadowlands while still remaining able to return to their body and resume life functions. Most of the ghosts encountered by Orpheus agents are of those who have passed on since the Maelstrom and don't have experience of the Dark Kingdoms.<br /> <br /> Orpheus doesn't use the same rules for wraithly Arcanoi. Instead the game has Horrors, paths of ghostly powers relating to a character's Shade, a kind of spectral psychological profile. The unspoken implication seems to be that the inexperienced ghosts are gradually rediscovering the same or similar principles as undergirded the Arcanoi, though. For example, the Haunter's path of Horrors has similar effects to various uses of the Inhabit Arcanos (it's one of two Shades whose starting Horrors actually share a name with a corresponding Arcanos, the other being the Skinrider and its starting power of Puppetry), and the later revealed Marrow Shade has Horrors with similar effects to Moliate. It's not a one-to-one correspondence; some Arcanoi aren't directly represented, and some Shades blend the themes of a few different Arcanoi.<br /> <br /> The rest of the game's rules run similarly: kind of an alternate mechanical interpretation of similar ideas, with Vitality standing in for both Corpus and Pathos, Spite for Angst, etc. Aside from the disappearance of wraiths familiar with the old culture of the Underworld, the Stormwall, and the emergence of a new sort of antagonist among the Malfeans, the biggest metaphysical difference is probably that ghosts modeled by Orpheus experience the Shadow as an exterior force. A spirit (the PC type that corresponds basically to a &quot;normal&quot; ghost rather than a living person) who isn't completely empty of Spite causes the existence of a spectre mirroring the spirit's personality, skills and powers, and basically driven by the same self-destructive id as the Shadow embodied in Wraith. If there's any kind of plot explanation for why that happens (as opposed to the obvious design explanation: Orpheus is a more cinematic and less directly introspective game, which is not a knock on it), I don't remember what it was.<br /> <br /> As for how it meshes with the Veil? It doesn't. The Orpheus Group's technology just kind of slices the Veil, and most of the wraiths who would have been able to counteract this happening have disappeared. Orpheus doesn't publicize everything it finds, and evidence of an afterlife doesn't mean they're able to start proving vampires or werewolves are real too or anything, but the Orpheus arc takes place in a world being jarred by a bizarre scientific discovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T19:39:20-07:00","id":685153,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. Also the Projectors and PC Ghosts, as presented in Orpheus, are on a lower power level than the other splats. So they're not really crossover friendly to begin with. Undoubtedly that will change in Wr20.<br /> <br /> Settingwise though it works okay. Orpheus is set post-6GM so we don't really have much of an idea on how Orpheus and the other Projection firms would interact with the wraiths of the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> If I had to say, publicly the Hierarchy would condemn interacting with Projectors on any level while behind the scenes they investigating these groups and thinking about how they can potentially use them or discredit and destroy the various firms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T22:10:17-07:00","id":685287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/685081-orpheus-and-wraiths?p=685147#post685147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orpheus doesn't publicize everything it finds, and evidence of an afterlife doesn't mean they're able to start proving vampires or werewolves are real too or anything, but the Orpheus arc takes place in a world being jarred by a bizarre scientific discovery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, I imagine Demons are happy about it. Dream Speakers, Taftani, Etherites, and Euthanatoi as well. Maybe even a few Void Engineers and Hunters.<br /> <br /> Heck, maybe they are the ones who were able to get this into the public eye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T05:46:42-07:00","id":685576,"title":"","content":"This question is one of the reasons I'm really looking forward to reading the Orpheus appendix of Wraith 20. It wasn't really addressed, which is fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T07:30:59-07:00","id":685729,"title":"","content":"In my personal head canon, the separation of spectres and spirits has two possible causes:<br /> <br /> 1. The 6GM increased the strength of Oblivion. As such, wraiths are no longer fractured spirits with one corpus, but shattered spirits with each fragment having its own corpus, meaning there are two (or perhaps three, if the Eidolon lingers) distinct soul shards doing their own thing. Or the spectres could simply be assuming the personality of Shadows now that Oblivion is once again able to self-generate Sparagmoi. But that would suggest wraiths still have Shadows too (which I don't think they do).<br /> <br /> 2. Orpheus, which presents things from the human POV, reflects the humans' flawed understanding of wraiths. They assumed the Shadow and Psyche were two separate beings, rather than recognising them as one being with a fractured soul.<br /> <br /> The former has some interesting possibilities, such as the possible appearance of an Eidolon self that can aid wraiths, but the latter is more easily aligned with Wraith as a corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T15:18:48-07:00","id":713089,"title":"","content":"Of course, Orpheus as a company in the setting was up and running not long after Project Flatline in early '96... The Sixth Great Maelstrom occured in '99... So projecting was happening before the Shadowlands got wrecked and the Shroud became the Stormwall. I expect that's what will be covered with Orpheus in Wraith20. I think going off the dates given in the metaplot that T&amp;S were up and running some time around '96 also... Which interestingly were part of the huge plan Bishop and Grandmaw made to spread Pigment.<br /> <br /> I ponder if in Wraith, that the Grandmaw was manifest as the Spectral Hive-Mind at that point. She was certainly dormant back then, but going off the dates given, clearly aligned with Bishop before the Ends of the Empire...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T13:26:03-07:00","id":739458,"title":"","content":"One of the nightmare scenarios our troupe feared was grandmother uncovering the gates of DtF's hell and chowing down on what was still inside and camping for slain fallen returning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:53:25-07:00","id":740522,"title":"","content":"I believe Orpheus had different rules than the rest of CWoD when it game to materializing as a ghost. In Wraith, IIRC it was terribly hard. In Orpheus, the ghosts are more like spirits in Exalted, they're immaterial but in our side of the world, but could materialize for instances. However ghosts could cross the Stormwall in Orpheus, but were basically trapped by the Gauntlet in Wraith. Mage and Werewolf also implied the samething IIRC for ghosts and other such things.<br /> <br /> I also could be remembering this incorrectly, but I'm almost positive it's true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T04:16:37-07:00","id":741293,"title":"","content":"Because Orpheus never sat down and stated exactly what each of its concepts was in relation to Wraith its a little hard to say what's going on. I believe the implication is that the 6th Great Maelstrom scoured the Shadowlands clean and pushed its way into the Gauntlet to create the night impenetrable Stormwall. Instead of being trapped in the Shadowlands unable to touch the world of the living, Ghosts are now trapped (dematerialized) in the Skinlands, unable to touch the world of the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}